    "result": "I replaced the fixed window in `limit.go` with a token bucket, but I could not run the tests. Every `go test` call needs approval, and this session gets no approval prompt.\n\n**API changes**\n- The signature is now `New(rate float64, burst int)`.\n- `AllowN(now, n)` is new, and `Tokens(now) float64` is new.\n\n**Behavior you did not specify**\n- `AllowN` with `n == 0` returns true and takes nothing. A negative `n` returns false.\n- `Tokens` only reads. It does not move the limiter's clock forward.\n- I did not add a mutex, because the old limiter did not have one. The limiter is not safe to call from several goroutines at once.\n\n**Tests**\n- In `limit_test.go`, I changed `TestAllow` to `New(1, 2)` to match the new signature.\n- I added tests for:\n  - refill and the cap at burst\n  - no burst at a second boundary\n  - an `AllowN` failure that takes nothing\n  - `n` above burst\n  - an earlier `now` that does not move the clock back\n\n**TLDR**\nThe limiter is now a token bucket and `New` takes `(rate float64, burst int)`. I could not run the tests, because `go test` needs an approval that this session cannot give. Run `go test ./...` yourself.",
